r nobody on file has, type the name if you know it and press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b>, or find the renter and press <b class="gd-ui">Link to</b> the name. The calls and texts so far follow the link. <b class="gd-ui">Match automatically again</b> undoes a link made by hand.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-missed-calls" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Missed calls</h2><p class="gd-p">A missed call raises the task &quot;Missed call from ...&quot; for the person on duty in customer service (whoever has Live chat or Texts and calls open), otherwise the customer service queue, and the Admins when nobody holds that function. In the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am) the task is due at 7 am. One open task per number.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Quo itself texts back missed callers (its own auto-reply). The platform can do it instead (Program settings, &quot;Missed call: text the caller back&quot;), once per number in 12 hours: turn off Quo&#39;s own auto-reply first, or callers get two texts.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-and-texts-on-records" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls and texts on records</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s page and a booking&#39;s Messages &amp; history section show the texts, calls, missed calls, voicemails and summaries in the Activity log (chips <b class="gd-ui">Texts</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b>); an owner&#39;s page has &quot;Calls and texts&quot;. Calls are recorded: each call has its transcript and a one-line summary in the Activity log, and calls placed from the site&#39;s Call button are recorded too (below).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-activity-log-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Activity log (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s page and a booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Messages &amp; history</b> section have one <b class="gd-ui">Activity</b> log: everything about the renter, newest first, grouped by day. It holds the emails and account messages both ways and the emails the platform sent, the texts, the live chat, the calls with their summaries and next steps, the notes, the booking&#39;s events, the payments and refunds, the documents, identity checks and signatures, and the visits to the site with what they did there and the signals.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">All</b> shows everything. Press a chip (Emails, Texts, Live chat, Calls, Notes, Booking, Payments, Documents and ID, Website) to see one type; press <b class="gd-ui">All</b> to go back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type in <b class="gd-ui">Search the activity</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Search</b> to find a word in the log; <b class="gd-ui">Clear</b> takes it away.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">50 lines show at a time: <b class="gd-ui">Older</b> shows the next 50, <b class="gd-ui">Newest</b> goes back to the top.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> are at the top of the log. An email from the renter has <b class="gd-ui">Reply</b>, a text or call from them <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>, a chat line <b class="gd-ui">Open the chat</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b> is above the log; the note shows in it at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Payments show to Admins, customer service, Sales and Finance, as the booking&#39;s Money section. The log never shows an email address or a phone number.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-quo-contacts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Quo contacts</h2><p class="gd-p">Everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, with their email and company: staff, renters and their drivers, owners, partners, investors, referral partners, job applicants, named visitors, leads, chauffeur clients, live chats, game players and forms left unfinished.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A new person is added within about five minutes; a changed name, phone or email is updated the same way. Change people on the site, not in Quo: the site&#39;s version is sent again.</li><li>One contact per number. When two records share a number, the strongest names the contact: staff, then a renter, a driver, an owner, a partner. A number without any name is not sent.</li><li>A contact someone already made in Quo for the number is updated rather than made twice, and its other numbers and emails are kept.</li><li>If Quo is down or slow, bookings and everything else go on; the contacts follow when it answers again.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Quo contacts</b>: how many are in Quo, waiting and in error, the last run and the last error, and <b class="gd-ui">Sync everyone again</b>. Program settings, &quot;Phone and texts (Quo)&quot;, turn it off.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-booking-texts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booking texts</h2><p class="gd-p">Since October 22, 2026 these are text alerts: each person chooses Email, Text or Both (the chapter Text alerts, below, and <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The settings</h2><p class="gd-p">Program settings, &quot;Phone and texts (Quo)&quot;: the line on or off, calls and texts kept, the missed-call text and its task, who calls back, AI suggestions and summaries with their daily neurons, the visit of a caller, and how long calls and texts of people who are not customers are kept (12 months).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-call-and-text-buttons" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call and Text buttons</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Call and Text button in Admin and the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map&#39;s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person&#39;s conversation under <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Texts and calls</b>; press <b class="gd-ui">Open the conversation</b> to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo&#39;s desktop app is your computer&#39;s calling app, tick <b class="gd-ui">On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app</b> once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To use the phone&#39;s own phone and messages apps instead, turn off <b class="gd-ui">Call and Text buttons go through Quo</b> in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone&#39;s own apps too.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-carmacars-app-links" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The CarmaCars app links</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, card The CarmaCars app (App Store and Google Play). Paste the App Store link (https://apps.apple.com/...) and the Google Play link (https://play.google.com/...) once the apps are live and press Save. From then on, iPhones and Android phones browsing the site see <b class="gd-ui">Download the CarmaCars app</b> in the footer and in the alerts invitation, with the link of their own store. Empty, nothing shows.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-who-is-calling-the-caller-pop-up-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who is calling: the caller pop-up (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">When someone calls the CarmaCars number, a panel opens at the bottom right of every Admin page (across the bottom on a phone) while the phone rings, and stays while the call goes on and for 3 minutes after it ends. Customer service get the same panel in their portal. The number is matched to the renter on file (their mobile or their account holder&#39;s), the same way Texts and calls matches it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A renter: their name, the booking on rent (or the next one coming) with the car, the balance they owe now (rental payments due and unpaid charges after a rental, <b class="gd-ui">overdue</b> when a payment is late), the deposit (held, waived, released, or not taken yet), what they are waiting on (a booking request or offer, a change, a question to them, an open To do) and the last three notes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write what the call was about in <b class="gd-ui">Note about this call</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b>: it is kept on the renter with the time, your name and the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Open the renter&#39;s page</b> opens the full record. The booking opens from its line.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An unknown number shows <b class="gd-ui">Unknown caller</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b> to keep it as a phone lead, then open the conversation in Texts and calls to name it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press the cross to close a call; it stays closed in this browser. The panel checks for calls every 10 seconds while you use the portal (once a minute when the page is left alone).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-renter-notes-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter notes (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter page has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b>, and its Activity log lists the notes (chip <b class="gd-ui">Notes</b>): what staff noted about the renter, newest first, with the date and time, who wrote it and their role, the booking and the words during a call when it was written from the pop-up. Admins and office staff add notes; nobody can change one. To take one away, press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> and give the reason: it is no longer shown, and the note, the removal and the reason stay in the audit log. The same notes show on the caller pop-up, on a renter&#39;s conversation in Texts and calls, and on the staff portal&#39;s renter.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-call-button-through-twilio-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Call button through Twilio (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Quo keeps incoming calls, texts and AI answering. <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a staff page rings the staff member&#39;s own cell, then connects the customer with the CarmaCars number as caller ID, and logs the call with its length and outcome on the renter, lead or booking. It needs the GitHub secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_API_KEY and TWILIO_API_SECRET (and the CarmaCars number as a verified caller ID in Twilio); until then <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> opens Quo and says why. A staff member with no mobile on their profile is asked for it the first time they press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> (a Canadian or US mobile, saved without a texted code), then the call starts (release 40).</p><p class="gd-p">Sales sees customer numbers hidden. Viewing as a Sales rep, <b class="gd-ui">Reveal</b> shows a number; every reveal is in the audit log.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-unanswered" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Unanswered</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Leads</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b> (customer service has it too): every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. <b class="gd-ui">Reply</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call back</b> opens the conversation; <b class="gd-ui">Mark answered</b> when it was answered another way. A customer waiting more than 15 minutes (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered SLA minutes</b>) alerts customer service and the Admins once. WhatsApp is not in the list: the morning digest reminds you to check it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-call-recording-and-transcripts-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call recording and transcripts (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Calls placed from the site&#39;s Call button are recorded from the moment the customer answers. No caller notice plays.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The recording is copied to CarmaCars&#39; private storage and deleted at Twilio once our copy is safe (Program settings, on by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">It is turned into text with the free daily AI allowance; when the allowance is used, the call waits for the next day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The transcript, its summary and Play recording show on the renter&#39;s, the lead&#39;s, the booking&#39;s and the conversation&#39;s history, for Admins, customer service and Sales.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The transcript feeds the renter&#39;s and the lead&#39;s intent at once (hot, warm or cold, with what they said they want).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Recording and deleting at Twilio are two switches in Program settings, under the phone settings.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'texts-and-calls', 'chapter', 'live-visitors-and-live-chat', 'Customer service and Sales answer texts to the CarmaCars number in the same place as live chat. Every call and text is kept with the renter, owner or lead it belongs to.

## Answer a text

1. Open **Visitors**, the **Chat** tab, and press **Texts and calls**. Unread texts and missed calls are counted on each number.
2. Choose a number: calls and texts in order, and beside them who it is, with their bookings.
3. Write the text and press **Send text**. It goes from the CarmaCars number.
4. **Suggest a reply** writes a draft into the box. Read it and change it: it is never sent until you press Send text.

## Unknown callers

Press **Unknown callers**. Type the name if they told you and press **Create lead**, or find the renter and press **Link to** their name.

Quo''s contacts follow the site: everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, added or updated within about five minutes. Change a name or number on the site, not in Quo: the site''s version is sent again.

## Missed calls

A missed call gives you the task "Missed call from ..." when you have Live chat or Texts and calls open; otherwise it waits in the customer service queue. Call back with the Call button, or text, then mark the task done. Quo itself texts the caller back, so do not send the same message again.

> Tip: A number that texted STOP gets no texts from us, booking texts included, until they text START. Prices go in a quote, never in a text from memory.

## Email, text or both

Each renter and owner chooses how we reach them. Their page in Admin shows it under How we reach them; ask an Admin, or change it there if you can open the page. Texts need a phone they verified with a code. Your own choice is on your Profile, under Messages.


## Call and Text buttons

Every Call and Text button in the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map''s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.

1. Press **Text**: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press **Send**. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person''s conversation under **Visitors** > **Chat** > **Texts and calls** (customer service and Sales); press **Open the conversation** to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.
2. Press **Call**: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo''s desktop app is your computer''s calling app, tick **On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app** once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.
3. Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.
4. An Admin can switch the buttons back to the phone''s own apps in Program settings. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone''s own apps too.

## Who is calling: the caller pop-up (release 34)

Customer service: when someone calls the CarmaCars number, a panel opens at the bottom right of every page of your portal (across the bottom on a phone) while the phone rings, and stays while the call goes on and for 3 minutes after it ends.

1. A renter: their name, the booking on rent (or the next one coming) with the car, the balance they owe now (**overdue** when a payment is late), the deposit (held, waived, released, or not taken yet), what they are waiting on (a request, an offer, a change, a question to them, an open To do) and the last three notes.
2. Write what the call was about in **Note about this call** and press **Add note**. It is kept on the renter with the time, your name and the booking.
3. **Open the renter''s page** opens their record. If it is outside your window, opening it from their call is logged as an opening for 24 hours with the reason Incoming call, as **Open with a reason** is.
4. An unknown number shows **Unknown caller**: press **Create lead** to keep it as a phone lead.
5. Press the cross to close a call; it stays closed in this browser.

## Renter notes (release 34)

A renter''s record (**Find a renter**, then Open) has **Add a note**, and the notes are in its Activity log (chip **Notes**), newest first, each with the date and time, who wrote it and their role. Add a note for every situation: what they asked, what you told them, what happens next. Notes cannot be changed or removed by staff, so write a new note to correct one; an Admin can remove a note with a reason. The notes also show on the caller pop-up and on a renter''s conversation in Texts and calls.

## Lanes, the Call button and hidden numbers (release 35)
1. Each conversation has a lane: **Fleet** for a car on rent, or a pickup, return, delivery or collection within a day; **Customer service** for the rest. The inbox has a tab for each. The caller pop-up rings for Fleet first on Fleet''s calls; customer service gets them when no Fleet staff member is on duty or nobody answered within 20 seconds.
2. **Call** rings your own phone first (the cell number in your profile). Answer it and we connect the customer, who sees the CarmaCars number. The call is noted on their history with its length. Until calling from the site is set up, **Call** opens Quo as before and says why.
3. Sales sees customer numbers hidden, like (647) •••-••00. Use **Call** and **Text** on the page: the number is found on our side. Search by phone still works.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.
